<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had harvested 22.8 percent of their 1996/997 wheat harvest by November 29, the Agriculture Secretariat said Thursday in its weekly crop report.</p>
<p>The wheat harvest has been helped by November's warm weather, which helped to mature the crop rapidly. Farmers had sown 32.5 percent of their soybean crop, compared with 50.7 percent sown at the same point last season. Maize sowing reached 78.5 percent, about the same level as last year. Sunflower sowing reached 87.2 percent, also about the same level as at the same point in 1995/96.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,873  100.0(100.0) 1,531.0   22.8  (13.5)   (18.9)</p>
<p> Maize     3,794   78.5 (80.7)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,313   32.5 (50.7)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,004   87.2 (89.4)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     770   56.6 (54.3)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	989   60.4  (n/a)     n/a    n/a   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
